  "channel_name": "Nick Puru | AI Automation",
  "transcript": "Google just officially killed [music] SEO. The way that you find customers online and the way that they find you just permanently changed forever. So, here's what happened. Over at Google's IO event, they rolled out the biggest shift in how people search in two decades. So, instead of giving you a bunch of links to scroll through, Google now answers you directly with AI overviews, the AI mode, and soon AI agents that are going to do the searching on your behalf. Nobody clicks on anything. And in Google's own words, links are about to become an afterthought. Now, AI overviews, they've already reached over 2 billion people a month, and AI mode, it's hitting hundreds of millions more. And within the year, AI will be the one researching your business for your customer. So, when nobody's clicking links, how do you actually get found? Well, this is the exact shift that we're walking our clients through right now. You quit [music] chasing the top spot that they used to click, and you start becoming the name that AI spits out when somebody asks. Which means that your reviews, your press, the Reddit threads about you, and every mention online now outweighs whatever's on your homepage. So, here's what you can do. Comment the word need, and I'll send you the free tool that shows everything AI is saying about you right now, the sources that it pulls from, and where your competitors actually show up and you don't. If you fix this in the next 90 days, you will own the next 10 years of search. And if you drag your feet, you'll just watch your leads quietly dry up with no idea what hit you.",
